<section class="section section--surface">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">What workflow automation does</p>
      <h2>The step after the finding, handled on its own.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="split">
      <div>
        <p>Most systems are good at capturing a problem and bad at making sure someone does something about it. <strong>Workflow Automation closes that gap:</strong> any event in the platform — a failed inspection, a form submission, a threshold breach — can trigger a task, an assignment, a notification, or an escalation, without anyone manually routing it.</p>
        <p>Rules run on conditions you set — asset criticality, location, requirement type — so the right person gets the right task, and nothing sits unassigned.</p>
        <ul class="tags tags--white"><li>Inspection answer trigger</li><li>Overdue task</li><li>Limit thresholds</li><li>Form submissions</li></ul>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/workflows/this-week-summary.webp" width="512" height="258" alt="This week: 38 tasks auto-created, 3 currently escalated, 0 unassigned. Automated: 21 inspections, 14 work orders, 3 compliance items." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2>Where a finding meets its follow-up.</h2>
      <p>Every event that matters moves through the same four stages — configured once, applied every time.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">01 — Rules</p>
        <h3>Rules &amp; triggers</h3>
        <p>Define what counts as an event worth acting on — a failed check, a missed threshold, a specific answer on a form — and what should happen next. No code required to configure a rule.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/workflows/rules-triggers.webp" width="512" height="277" alt="Rule for a failed containment check, active on containment inspections: BMP failure escalates. Trigger: inspection result is Fail. Condition: asset criticality is High. Action: create a task and notify the supervisor." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">02 — Assignment</p>
        <h3>Assignment &amp; routing</h3>
        <p>Tasks route to the right person automatically — matched by role, location, or who's on shift — instead of landing in a shared inbox and waiting for someone to claim them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/workflows/assignment-routing.webp" width="512" height="278" alt="Task TSK-3391 assigned: repair containment berm B-12, auto-routed by location and role to M. Ortega, field supervisor, matched to Dry Creek Pad, due within 24 hours." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">03 — Escalation</p>
        <h3>Escalation paths</h3>
        <p>If a task isn't acted on in time, it escalates on its own — to a supervisor, then a manager — following the path you define. Nothing quietly ages out past its deadline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/workflows/escalation-paths.webp" width="512" height="314" alt="Escalation for TSK-3391: assigned to M. Ortega at 7:15 AM, due in 24 hours with no action taken, SLA breached and escalated to the ops manager, manager notified and awaiting acknowledgment." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="capability capability--flip">
      <div>
        <p class="card-kicker">04 — History</p>
        <h3>Full audit trail</h3>
        <p>Every automated action is logged — who was assigned, when it escalated, who closed it out. When the auditor asks who knew what and when, the answer is already written down.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="capability-media">
        <img src="/static/img/workflows/audit-trail.webp" width="531" height="313" alt="Audit log for TSK-3391: task created automatically at 7:14 AM, assigned to M. Ortega at 7:15 AM, escalated to the ops manager at 9:02 AM, manager notified at 9:04 AM. Every entry logged automatically." loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

